# Shared-node affinity consumer contract

**Activation:** `alwaysApply: false` — when triggers in `agent-discipline-core.mdc` match, **Read this file before editing**. Triggered rules are mandatory, not optional.

How (discovery, GPU index, ingest order): `.cursor/plans/shared-node-affinity-wiring.plan.md`. This rule is the consumer invariant.

## Wire

```text
%jobs jids=<jid1,jid2,...>
%affinity jid=<jid> cpus=<csv-or-ranges> gpus=<csv-or-> cg=<short-optional>
```

Sample header stays one jobid token. Unknown `%` lines (`%begin`, `%end`) stay ignored.

**Detect shared-node contract** from **`%jobs` with at least one jid** — not from hostname, INI, or “this host runs the shared-node RPM.” Sole full-resource jobs (monitor omits both marks when one jid has all online CPUs **and** all available GPUs) look identical to exclusive file-mode samples; do **not** invent membership or `dev=j:` for them.

**Monitor mark emit (consumer expects):**

| Case | Marks |
| --- | --- |
| Sole jid, full CPU **and** full GPU | neither `%jobs` nor `%affinity` |
| Full CPU but not all GPUs (or reverse) | `%jobs` + `%affinity` when known |
| Sole partial jid | `%jobs jids=<that jid>` (+ `%affinity` when known) |

## Side table

- `job_affinity`: normal table, unique `(jid, host)`. `cgroup_controls` is provenance (`cg=`), not a cgroup path.
- No second hypertable. Job membership for a sample is `host_data` itself.
- No `host_data` UNIQUE / PK migration. Do not store a jid CSV in `host_data.jid`.

## Stamp

After a shared sample header whose jid is not `-`, non-GPU rows get `dev=j:<jid>` **before** collapse and collapse keeps that token in the group key. GPU types keep hardware `dev`. Exclusive payloads and sole full-resource payloads (no `%jobs`) still collapse to `dev=''`.

## AMQP multi-header bodies

Monitor may merge up to 10 non-`$` ring entries into one AMQP body. Attach `%jobs` / `%affinity` to the **digit header block they precede**, not to the whole body. Idle `-` blocks in the same body keep `dev=''`. Regression: `test_multi_header_amqp_body_binds_marks_per_block`.

Listend and sync_timedb (line parse and streaming) call the same helper. Writes are idempotent and fail-open when `job_affinity` is absent. No `/api/affinity/ingest/`.

## Read paths

`LiveJidScopedDistinctHostTimeCount` matches `host_data.jid` or `host_data.dev = 'j:' || job.jid`. `update_metrics` readiness uses the same two keys via `max_host_time_by_jid`. Exclusive jobs match the `jid` column and keep `dev=''`.

## Deploy

Migration `0036` and this consumer land before a monitor built with `--enable-shared-node-multi-jid`. File-mode monitors and `/var/run/stats_jobid` stay valid.
